# Random modules with existentially typed predicates and functions, some
# with existential constraints, and existentially typed constructors,
# whose callers use what they get as they use their own type variables'
# values, pass it to constrained callees, give it back as their own
# existentially typed outputs, and construct with 'new'
# (generate-polymorphic-programs.py --existentials). merkc must give each
# procedure the hidden arguments mmc does, outputs among them, make each
# clause give the same type_infos and typeclass_infos for its existential
# types, and pass and get the same at each call, construction and
# deconstruction.
#
# REQUIRES: mmc
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir %t
# RUN: %python %S/../../../utils/type-oracle/generate-polymorphic-programs.py --existentials --seed 27 --count 40 %t
# RUN: %compare-polymorphism %t/*.m
